# case 15: an anti join over the joined rows: MySQL buffers the rows of all the tables (the join buffer is small, so it spills them to disk)
42:94736792227
EXPLAIN FORMAT=TREE SELECT f.id, d1.a FROM f_w f JOIN d1_w d1 ON f.k1 = d1.k WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM f_w g WHERE g.k1 = f.k1 AND g.v <> d1.b AND g.id < f.id);
EXPLAIN
-> Hash antijoin (g.k1 = f.k1), extra conditions: (g.v <> d1.b) and (g.id < f.id)
    -> Nested loop inner join
        -> Table scan on f, with parallel hash join
        -> Table scan on d1, joined by the parallel hash join
    -> Hash
        -> Table scan on g

